Package: AlphaForgeInsightBackend
Type: Package
Title: AlphaForge Insight R/Plumber Backend
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Nipun Anand", "Saxena", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Backend REST API for the AlphaForge Insight Quant Strategy
    Backtester (Review 1, VIT Software Engineering Project). Phase 1
    scaffold implemented the GET /health liveness endpoint. Phase 2 adds
    database persistence (Neon PostgreSQL via DBI/RPostgres) and
    authentication (bcrypt password hashing, JWT via jose):
    POST /auth/register, POST /auth/login, GET /auth/me.
    Phase 3 adds the market-data + technical-indicator layer
    (quantmod/TTR/xts): GET /stocks/validate and GET /market-data, with
    SMA/RSI indicator functions (generic periods).
    Phase 4 adds the strategy engine: centralized validation with documented
    defaults (STRATEGY_DEFAULTS), MA-crossover/RSI crossing signal generation
    (no look-ahead), GET /strategies/defaults and JWT-protected
    POST /strategies/preview.
    Phase 5 adds the pure backtesting engine and performance-metric layer:
    backend/analytics/execution.R (t+1-open execution, cash/shares tracking,
    trade log, equity curve, open-position handling, run_backtest
    orchestration) and backend/analytics/metrics.R (Total Return, CAGR,
    Sharpe, Sortino, Maximum Drawdown, Win Rate, Volatility, Total Trades).
    No API endpoints are added in Phase 5; /backtest/run arrives in Phase 6.
    Phase 7 adds the Feature-Engineering + ML/DL module
    (backend/analytics/ml/): leak-free feature construction, supervised
    BUY/HOLD/SELL labels, chronological splitting, 12 models (logistic
    regression, LDA, QDA, KNN, naive Bayes, decision tree, random forest,
    SVM, gradient boosting, XGBoost, MLP, LSTM) behind a common interface,
    classification + trading evaluation, and a probability-based Top-N
    portfolio adapter feeding the EXISTING t+1-open backtesting engine via
    the new JWT-protected /ml/features, /ml/train, /ml/compare, /ml/predict
    and /ml/backtest endpoints.
    Later phases add the backtesting engine,
    performance metrics and persistence.
